==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Papalan Pasalan''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Sukelan Kakulan''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
This form is <u>useless by design</u>. Similarly to the other cats from Tales of the Nekoluga, this Cat is not meant to be used until it evolves.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Although the Curse ability might sound exciting, it's impractical if not outright useless in most scenarios because it only shuts off certain enemy abilities, which barely hinders them for the most part. Furthermore, Papalan Pasalan's Curse has terrible uptime, which potentially enables said abilities to activate anyway unless other units eliminate these threats, which defeats the point of even using him in the first place. As with many units in his set, Papalan Pasalan will perish to whatever that hits him, making him vulnerable to many [[:Category:Long Distance Enemies|Long Distance]]/[[:Category:Omni Strike Enemies|Omni Strike]]/[[:Category:Wave Attack Enemies|Wave]]/[[:Category:Surge Attack Enemies|Surge]]/[[:Category:Explosion Enemies|Explosion]] enemies, and his long recharge time means he won't return quickly enough to make a difference.

==='''True Form'''===
Sukelan Kakulan's most notable buff is complete immunity to [[Surge Attack|Surges]]. This is an improvement, but it only really means that Sukelan won't directly die to Surges that spawn in his position; a Surge spawning on him would still mean problems to the units that are supposed to protect him, which are fundamental due to his low survivability. Only resistant meatshields, a [[Cat Combo]]-buffed [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]], [[Talents|Talented]] [[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Gato Amigo]], or [[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cat Cactus]] function as a valid defense, while even less cats may work as mid-ranged attackers against Surges, leading to a quick demise for Sukelan. However, Sukelan Kakulan can still find use in certain occasions. For example, he can disable [[Red EnerG]]'s Knockback ability, preventing any Surges from pushing [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cats]] that are meant to tank said enemy while avoiding them himself. Nevertheless, it's important to mention these matchups are ultimately situational, and don't expand his utility much.

In addition to Surge immunity and an irrelevant improvement to his still-pitiful health, his Curse lasts for one second longer, but he still doesn't come close to having 100% uptime. On top of all that, Sukelan requires both an Elder [[Catfruit]] and a Gold Catfruit Seed to evolve, making this True Form evolution nearly useless outside of collection.

==='''Talents'''===
Unfortunately, Sukelan Kakulan has almost no utility, meaning any investment in his Talents will be a complete waste, as his stats and cooldown are simply too much for most players to handle. The only somewhat justifiable Talent is Survive. While this does help with his long cooldown, the investment doesn't offer any return for keeping him in action.

