==Trivia==
*Papaluga's Japanese name, Oiruga (オイルガ), is derived from おいる ''oiru'', meaning "growing old".
*Papaluga and [[Furiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Furiluga]] are the only [[Tales of the Nekoluga (Gacha Event)|Lugas]] whose Normal Forms' English and Japanese names are entirely different from one another.
*Sukelan Kakulan is a reference to Mitsuemon, the false identity of Tokugawa Mitsukuni in the long-running period drama ''[[wikipedia:Mito Kōmon|Mito Kōmon]]''. Both have white beards, wear the same accessories, and use a cane as a weapon. His name comes from Suke-san and Kaku-san, Mitsukuni's samurai retainers.
**Papaluga is the only Luga whose [[True Form]] references a television drama.
*Papaluga and [[Kaoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Kaoluga]] are the only Lugas whose True Form's English names don't have "Pasalan" in them.

